      "id": 1,
      "text": "La Habra Heights was founded in 1896 and originally called La Habra when a post office opened in a corner store.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lahabraca.gov/531/History",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "During the ranchos era, Don Mariano Reyes Roldan received 6,698 acres and named the land Rancho Cañada de La Habra.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lahabraca.gov/531/History",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1913, La Habra turned into a \"tent city\" as oil and citrus workers flooded the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lahabraca.gov/531/History",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Walter Beck, the Heights’ resident, became a leading expert on avocado cultivation, shaping the region’s agricultural reputation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
